#N canvas 20 20 3060 520 12;
#X text 20 20 bench-tap -- loaded BESIDE a bench so a step can assert on what actually reached a bus. IT LISTENS AND SENDS NOTHING \, which is what makes it safe: g_oled owns oscOut and g_grid owns the grid \, but that governs WRITING -- Pd delivers a message to EVERY receiver of a name \, so adding one here cannot change what any other subscriber sees. ⛔ DO NOT ROUTE ITS OUTPUT ANYWHERE. clock is deliberately absent: two beats a second forever \, which no assertion wants and which would bury every window it appeared in., f 120;
#X text 20 150 ⛔ THIS FILE IS AN OUTPUT. Edit build_tap in test/bench/bench-gen.py and regenerate \; never this. The print labels are lib_drive.TAP_LABELS \, which is the same map test/gate/lib_assert.py's parser matches -- so the runner reuses the gates' parser rather than growing a second one., f 120;
